    ('109801f8-e5f8-48eb-8705-5b413b582d59', 6, $$Leela can’t wait to ride to school now!$$),
    ('109801f8-e5f8-48eb-8705-5b413b582d59', 7, $$$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 0, $$The durians in Nani's orchard have started to fall.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 1, $$Nani collects the fallen durian fruits.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 2, $$Nani backpacks the durian fruit back home.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 3, $$Nani splits the durian and then eats it.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 4, $$Nani splits one more durian because she still wants to eat.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 5, $$The remaining durian flesh that are not eaten are placed in a container.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 6, $$The container filled with durian is stored inside the refrigerator.$$),
    ('150e82e8-e14d-41af-a897-28d5816a42cb', 7, $$The other durian fruits are sold at the market.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 0, $$Everyone knows that the elephant has a very long nose.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 1, $$But a long time ago, the elephant’s nose was short and fat. Like a shoe in the middle of his face.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 2, $$A curious baby elephant was born. She had a question for every animal.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 3, $$She was curious about Giraffe. “Why do you have a long neck? ” she asked.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 4, $$She was curious about Rhino. “Why does your horn have a sharp point? ”$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 5, $$She was curious about Hippo. “Why do you have red eyes? ” she asked.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 6, $$And she was VERY curious about Crocodile. “What does Crocodile eat for dinner? ”$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 7, $$“Never ask a question like that! ” said her mother. She walked off, frowning.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 8, $$But clever Crow quickly said, “Follow me to the river. There you will see what Crocodile eats for dinner. ”$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 9, $$So Baby Elephant followed Crow all the way down to the river.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 10, $$She pushed through the reeds and stood on the bank. She looked into the water. Where was Crocodile?$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 11, $$“Hello,” said a stone near the river bank. “Hello,” said Baby Elephant. “Perhaps you can tell me what Crocodile eats for dinner? ”$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 12, $$“Bend down and I will tell you,” said the stone. “Lower, lower... ” So Baby Elephant bent down lower, until…$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 13, $$“Snap! ” Her nose was in the jaws of Crocodile. “Crocodile will eat you for dinner! ” squawked Crow.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 14, $$Baby Elephant sat back on her strong legs and pulled, and pulled, and pulled. But Crocodile did not let go.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 15, $$Baby Elephant’s nose stretched, and stretched, and stretched, until… “Duuffff! ” she fell on her back.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 16, $$Cross at losing his dinner, Crocodile slithered back into the water.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 17, $$Baby Elephant looked at her nose. She could not see where it ended!$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 18, $$It was so long she could pick fruit from high branches.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 19, $$And shower herself with water on a hot day.$$),
    ('1ac0266a-60eb-4838-a25c-68ff3d5ebbae', 20, $$And to this day, all elephants have very long and useful trunks.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 0, $$Goat, Dog and Cow were great friends. One day they went on a journey in a taxi.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 1, $$They reached the end of their journey. The driver asked them to pay their fares. Cow paid her fare.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 2, $$Dog paid extra, because he did not have the correct money.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 3, $$The driver was about to give Dog his change, when suddenly Goat ran away without paying.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 4, $$The driver was very annoyed. He drove away without giving Dog his change.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 5, $$That is why, even today, Dog runs toward a car to peep inside. He is looking for the driver who owes him change.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 6, $$Goat runs away from the sound of a car. She is afraid she will be arrested for not paying her fare.$$),
    ('1e05b104-7886-4654-829e-29863d35b831', 7, $$And Cow is not bothered by cars. Cow takes her time crossing the road. She knows she paid her fare in full.$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 0, $$Hello, I am the fourth one in the line. Can you see me?$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 1, $$Left, right, left, right. We walk silently in a line.$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 2, $$I just got an idea. I am going to get a set of WHEELS to move faster!$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 3, $$We are not noisy like other animals. Ours is a language of smells.$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 4, $$One kind of smell says, “Follow me this way for a feast. ”$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 5, $$Another smell says, “Danger! Do not go there. ”$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 6, $$I love cakes and all kinds of sweets, just like you.$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 7, $$Want to see my muscles at work? I may look very tiny to you, but I am very strong.$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 8, $$Never mind if the door is shut. I can slip through the smallest crack.$$),
    ('22785a51-5eeb-421f-a52d-0e1fa47ad35f', 9, $$Believe it or not, hundreds of us live happily in a colony.$$),
    ('22e8ca3b-9cb6-465a-b3ab-5eb0753aab92', 0, $$I dance when I am happy, I dance when I am sad, I dance when I am lonely, I dance when I am mad.$$),
    ('22e8ca3b-9cb6-465a-b3ab-5eb0753aab92', 1, $$My teacher says, “Sit still! Don’t dance about all day. ”$$),
    ('22e8ca3b-9cb6-465a-b3ab-5eb0753aab92', 2, $$But my mother says, "Dancing makes you healthy, Dancing makes you tall, One day you'll be a dancer, And surprise them all! "$$),
    ('22e8ca3b-9cb6-465a-b3ab-5eb0753aab92', 3, $$And I say, "One day I'll dance And people will pay Just to see me leap and twirl.$$),
    ('22e8ca3b-9cb6-465a-b3ab-5eb0753aab92', 4, $$"'Her dancing is SO good,' They'll say. "$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 0, $$I love water.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 1, $$I enjoy playing with water.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 2, $$It is raining.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 3, $$It is raining. We collect water, and are glad for it.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 4, $$I enjoy playing outside.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 5, $$But it is raining.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 6, $$I enjoy playing out in the rain.$$),
    ('232b4859-e9d8-497b-90bd-d4d6d1d8e038', 7, $$My hair is wet from playing in the rain. My father is fixing my hair.$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 0, $$Kicchu woke up early one morning. “It is time to catch some fish,” he said yawning.$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 1, $$He met Choru on the way to the pond. They were best friends who played all day long.$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 2, $$Munia saw them marching with their fishing rods. “We are going to the pond to catch fish. Come along Munia, if you wish. ”$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 3, $$Little Munia thought for sometime. “Please don’t do that,” she said, “without water, the fish will die. ”$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 4, $$They did not listen to what Munia had to say. They headed to the pond straight away.$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 5, $$Kicchu and Choru sat waiting by the pond. Two fish swam across, one thin and another round.$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 6, $$Then came the third fish, the biggest one they had seen. Munia said laughing, “It is bigger than Appa’s feet! ”$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 7, $$Kicchu and Choru held on tight to their rods. Kicchu screamed, “MY FISH! ” Choru also screamed, “NO... MY FISH! ”$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 8, $$Kicchu pulled hard... Choru pulled harder...$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 9, $$PHAAATTT! Both the rods broke. THUDDD! Kicchu fell to the ground. SSSPPLAASH! Choru fell into the water.$$),
    ('24b31158-0cda-4ef3-a7c9-faa9903073d5', 10, $$What had happened? What do you think? The fish had tied up both the strings!$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 0, $$My Amma tells me a story every night.$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 1, $$There is one story about a frog which talks.$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 2, $$There is another story about a king with a long beard.$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 3, $$Sometimes it is about a flying elephant.$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 4, $$In one story a fox and a tiger are friends. The tiger falls into a hole.$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 5, $$How will the tiger get out?$$),
    ('27a68d85-2143-46a9-9817-d6d026a2a020', 6, $$Then the clever fox saves the tiger. This is the best story. I listen to the story and then fall asleep.$$),
    ('293fbcf7-33f8-4807-8040-e71d3b9255d4', 0, $$One evening Tintu was playing with his garden friends.$$),
    ('293fbcf7-33f8-4807-8040-e71d3b9255d4', 1, $$He was enjoying the bird's play and suddenly...$$),
    ('293fbcf7-33f8-4807-8040-e71d3b9255d4', 2, $$A beetle called Tintu and asked him to feed it with something delicious.$$),
    ('293fbcf7-33f8-4807-8040-e71d3b9255d4', 3, $$Tintu rushed home and took some vegetables.$$),
    ('293fbcf7-33f8-4807-8040-e71d3b9255d4', 4, $$He made a tasty and yummy soup.$$),
    ('293fbcf7-33f8-4807-8040-e71d3b9255d4', 5, $$The beetle was happy to taste the soup.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 0, $$I am a big girl. I go out of the house alone.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 1, $$It is so dark! Is someone there? Who is it?$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 2, $$Oh, it is only the cat. I am not afraid.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 3, $$I can see a big dark thing outside! What is it?$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 4, $$Oh, it is only the well. I am not afraid.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 5, $$And that sound! Creak creak creak! What is it?$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 6, $$Only my sister drawing water from the well! I am not afraid.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 7, $$I hear footsteps! Who is it? Who is it?$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 8, $$It is my mother. She has come home from the fields.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 9, $$I am a big girl now.$$),
    ('2c38efe1-cfa2-4690-a9df-c1dce34cd251', 10, $$I am not afraid of anything!$$),
    ('2c6ce11c-66a8-40c1-bc82-1e9be8410301', 0, $$This baby goat is little and white. I love to play with them.$$),
    ('2c6ce11c-66a8-40c1-bc82-1e9be8410301', 1, $$My sister and I like to spend time with our goats in the winter.$$),
    ('2c6ce11c-66a8-40c1-bc82-1e9be8410301', 2, $$I like feeding them with milk from a baby bottle.$$),
    ('2c6ce11c-66a8-40c1-bc82-1e9be8410301', 3, $$My sister's goat is black and white. It is growing very fast.$$),
    ('2c6ce11c-66a8-40c1-bc82-1e9be8410301', 4, $$See the horns. They are very long and hard. It likes to butt when the dog gets near it.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 0, $$Air is always around us. Moving air is called wind. When wind blows, it carries energy.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 1, $$The wind’s energy can lift kites into the sky.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 2, $$When something resists the wind’s movement, its energy can build up...$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 3, $$before releasing in a violent burst.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 4, $$But we can also capture the wind’s energy and change it into energy that we can use.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 5, $$Turbines help us transform wind energy into electrical energy.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 6, $$And the spinning blades change wind energy into electricity.$$),
    ('2e5d2a58-7ab9-4694-baeb-806fe7ec10f2', 7, $$We can use this electricity long after the wind stops blowing.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 0, $$All of us went to the fun fair.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 1, $$Father bought brother fancy glasses. Mother bought me a bright blue cap. The baby got sugar candy.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 2, $$On the way home, a very strong wind came. It blew my cap away.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 3, $$My cap got stuck on a branch of a big old tree.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 4, $$I cried a lot. And I did not eat my dinner.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 5, $$Later that night, the moon came up. It looked at my cap in the big old tree.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 6, $$The moon tried on my cap. It smiled happily. I had to smile too.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 7, $$$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 8, $$After school the next day, my mother gave me a shiny new red cap. "The moon sent it," she said.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 9, $$That night, both the moon and I wore our caps and smiled. We were happy.$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 10, $$Do you think the sun needs a hat?$$),
    ('314b2bd9-4328-407b-8383-452e32a807eb', 11, $$Guess which cap I am wearing today!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 0, $$Take the ball!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 1, $$Put down the pencil!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 2, $$Give me the paper!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 3, $$Touch the chair!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 4, $$Take the bowl!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 5, $$Put down the book!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 6, $$Give me the drinking glass!$$),
    ('352529f5-f5f1-44fd-b66f-222f7bfb7309', 7, $$Touch the table!$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 0, $$Pip the pup had a dream. "I want to go to space! " said Pip. He got in his red rocket.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 1, $$First, Pip saw Mercury . "It's so hot here! " said Pip. He waved and flew on.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 2, $$Next came Venus . "So bright and full of clouds! " Pip smiled and zoomed away.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 3, $$Then Pip saw a blue and green ball. "It's Earth ! My home! " He gave it a big hug.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 4, $$Mars was red and dry. Pip saw big rocks and dust. "No pups here," he said.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 5, $$"Wow! " said Pip at Jupiter . "It's so big! And look at the big red spot! " He flew around the giant planet.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 6, $$Next was Saturn with its rings. "They look like hula hoops! " Pip did a loop-de-loop.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 7, $$Uranus was blue and cold. Pip wore a coat. "Brr! " he said.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 8, $$Last was Neptune . "The wind is strong here! " Pip held on tight.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 9, $$Time to go home.$$),
    ('37f47916-0ca4-427f-8e09-83e74a369399', 10, $$"I saw all 8 planets! " said Pip. He zoomed back to bed. "Good nigt, space! "$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 0, $$Sun$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 1, $$Moon$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 2, $$Birds$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 3, $$Lightning$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 4, $$Rain$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 5, $$Clouds$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 6, $$Airplane$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 7, $$Smoke$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 8, $$Rainbow$$),
    ('38b2f0c5-46a4-4792-9ee2-eb389488a26f', 9, $$Stars$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 0, $$I am a big boy now. I can draw and I can make things.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 1, $$I draw my mother, she sits still.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 2, $$I draw my sister, she does not sit still.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 3, $$I draw many things.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 4, $$But I am told not to draw on the wall.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 5, $$I can make things.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 6, $$I make a drawing of a cat, she is fat.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 7, $$I make a fish. It is small.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 8, $$I make paper boats, birds and planes.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 9, $$I make houses and trains.$$),
    ('39382464-4b77-488c-8fd6-a079dc7eaa22', 10, $$My sister makes a mess! I can make many things. But my sister cannot!$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 0, $$This is a claw.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 1, $$This is a feather.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 2, $$This is a hoof.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 3, $$This is a horn.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 4, $$This is a tail.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 5, $$This is fur.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 6, $$This is a wing.$$),
    ('39b34ff9-4c9b-48db-8104-71655e93b463', 7, $$This is a beak.$$),
    ('3b9944ca-2137-4101-a390-bf3ed5b505e1', 0, $$This person is a man.$$),
