    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 0, $$Some wild cats have stripes. Like the tiger!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 1, $$Some wild cats have manes. Like the lion!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 2, $$Some wild cats have spots. Like the leopard and the leopard cat!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 3, $$Some wild cats are the best climbers. Like the clouded leopard and the marbled cat!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 4, $$Some wild cats live high up in the mountains. Like the snow leopard and the Pallas's cat!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 5, $$Some wild cats live in the desert. Like the desert cat!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 6, $$Some wild cats love to fish. Like the fishing cat.$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 7, $$Some wild cats are the smallest wild cats in the world. Like the rusty-spotted cat!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 8, $$Some wild cats look like house cats. Like the jungle cat and the golden cat!$$),
    ('3c0d7564-4c97-4d80-8214-29c4af72d35e', 9, $$But they are all wild cats!$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 0, $$My village had many problems. We made a long line to fetch water from one well.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 1, $$We waited under one big tree for food donated by others.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 2, $$We locked our houses early because of theft.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 3, $$Many children dropped out of school.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 4, $$Young girls worked as maids in other villages.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 5, $$Young boys roamed around the village, while others worked on people's farms.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 6, $$When the wind blew, waste paper hung on trees and fences.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 7, $$People were cut by broken glass that was thrown carelessly.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 8, $$Then one day, the well dried up and our water containers were empty.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 9, $$My father walked from house to house calling people to attend a village meeting.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 10, $$People gathered under the big tree where we had got donated food.$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 11, $$My father stood in the middle of the group. He said, “We need to solve the problems in our village. We need to work together. ”$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 12, $$Eight-year-old Juma, sitting on a tree trunk shouted, “I can help with cleaning up. ”$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 13, $$One middle-aged woman said, “The women can join me to grow food. ”$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 14, $$Another man stood up and said, “The men will dig a well for water. ”$$),
    ('3f87bf86-11c0-49fa-8966-63cff7ed0f28', 15, $$We all shouted with one voice, “We must change our lives. ” From that day we worked together and solved our problems.$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 0, $$Where is the ant?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 1, $$Where is the snail?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 2, $$Where is the mouse?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 3, $$Where is the bird?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 4, $$Where is the lizard?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 5, $$Where is the cat?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 6, $$Where is the hen?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 7, $$Where is the dog?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 8, $$Where is the pig?$$),
    ('409a37a2-27aa-4bae-8421-8aafeab23bf6', 9, $$Where is the goat?$$),
    ('40b14297-e2c9-4977-b222-cc00cc9f6cce', 0, $$The bird is on the chair.$$),
    ('40b14297-e2c9-4977-b222-cc00cc9f6cce', 1, $$The bird is in front of the chair.$$),
    ('40b14297-e2c9-4977-b222-cc00cc9f6cce', 2, $$The bird is under the chair.$$),
    ('40b14297-e2c9-4977-b222-cc00cc9f6cce', 3, $$The bird is behind the chair.$$),
    ('40b14297-e2c9-4977-b222-cc00cc9f6cce', 4, $$The bird is next to the chair.$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 0, $$Jesus’ disciples said to him, “Send the crowds away so they can buy food. ”$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 1, $$“They don’t need to go. You give them something to eat,” Jesus said.$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 2, $$They said, “We have only five loaves and two fish. ”$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 3, $$“Bring them here to me,” Jesus replied.$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 4, $$Jesus gave thanks and the disciples gave the food to the crowds.$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 5, $$Everyone ate and was satisfied. Those who ate were more than five thousand.$$),
    ('410ca735-a70e-4b36-8899-aa4ab41a1127', 6, $$$$),
    ('411f6dd4-ade3-4c44-b443-0cf3646ba3bb', 0, $$Anna is a smiling young girl with blonde hair and she is sitting in a wheelchair.$$),
    ('411f6dd4-ade3-4c44-b443-0cf3646ba3bb', 1, $$These are some of my friends. We like to go on adventures together.$$),
    ('411f6dd4-ade3-4c44-b443-0cf3646ba3bb', 2, $$There are several children gathered around a table looking at a piece of paper. There are a few children just outside the door looking in.$$),
    ('411f6dd4-ade3-4c44-b443-0cf3646ba3bb', 3, $$The group of children are gathered by a door putting on hats. Many are wearing sunglasses.$$),
    ('411f6dd4-ade3-4c44-b443-0cf3646ba3bb', 4, $$Anna is pointing to a bottle her friend is holding while standing near a storage closet.$$),
    ('411f6dd4-ade3-4c44-b443-0cf3646ba3bb', 5, $$We decided to go to the fair. Oh, what a fun day it will be!$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 0, $$One day I went to the garden with Mama and Papa. We walked past a stream and a big water fall.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 1, $$While Mama and Papa worked, I saw a big , beautiful butterfly.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 2, $$I loved the bright colours on the wings of the butterfly.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 3, $$I followed the butterfly everywhere. I wanted to catch the butterfly, but it flew away over the waterfall.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 4, $$I realised I was lost and could not see Mama or Papa anymore. I was afraid.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 5, $$Mama and Papa could not hear me crying. I didn´t know what to do.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 6, $$I looked at the waterfall, then I had an idea. Follow the water back up , I thought. The water will take me back to the garden.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 7, $$I began to follow the stream up the mountain, and then, in the distance, I could see the village gardens .$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 8, $$I was so happy. My father and mother saw me from far away, and came quickly for me. They carried me back to the garden.$$),
    ('41e96c26-70a0-4341-8560-c9ab638b1aba', 9, $$Over my father's shoulder, I saw the bright butterfly fly by and wave its wings at me.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 0, $$I am a big girl. I can help other people.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 1, $$After school, I like to feed my little brother. He loves it.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 2, $$When I have a holiday, I help my mother get ready to go to the office.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 3, $$In the evening, I help my father in his shop.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 4, $$But sometimes my mother says, "Please, do not help me! "$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 5, $$And sometimes my father says, "Thank you, but please do not help me today. "$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 6, $$Sometimes they both tell me to sit in one place.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 7, $$I like to help my grandmother. She tells me stories.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 8, $$My brother is still small.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 9, $$But I am a big girl.$$),
    ('43f98ac5-0061-40a5-969e-dbec2f5d6cb4', 10, $$I can help other people.$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 0, $$“What am I going to do? ” Kunga asked his friend, Foxy. “My favourite jacket disappeared! ” “Where did it go? ” asked Foxy.$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 1, $$“We washed it this morning and I helped my Mum hang it on the line,” Kunga said. “But when I came back it was gone. ”$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 2, $$“Show me,” said Foxy. “See,” said Kunga. “It’s gone…”$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 3, $$“Look, there are prints,” shouted Foxy. “Let’s follow them. ”$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 4, $$Kunga and Foxy followed the prints around the pond.$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 5, $$They followed the prints through the grass.$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 6, $$And across the river but then the prints stopped. “Oh, no, where did they go? Kunga asked.$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 7, $$$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 8, $$There on a big rock stood a goat and in his mouth was… my jacket.$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 9, $$“You naughty goat,” Kunga called. “That’s my jacket. Give it back. ” “Don’t hurt me,” cried the goat. “Sorry, sorry. There is your jacket. ”$$),
    ('442fd0c3-a935-4d65-9ca9-33602df5f660', 10, $$“Great,” said Kunga. “We solved the mystery,” grinned Foxy.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 0, $$Today I am not going to school.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 1, $$It is a holiday!$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 2, $$Today I am not going to watch TV.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 3, $$There is no electricity anyway.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 4, $$What am I going to do?$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 5, $$Today I am going to listen to my body!$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 6, $$First, I have to be quiet. Very quiet. So that I can listen to my own body.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 7, $$Yes, now I can hear my breath. In... out... in... out...$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 8, $$And I can make my breath noisier... Ssssssssssssss! And softer... Mmmmmmm.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 9, $$And now I can hear my heart beating! Doodom, doodoom, dooodooom.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 10, $$Can I make my heart go faster or louder? Yes, by jumping up and down twenty times.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 11, $$Now see, my heart is beating faster. Doodom, doodoom, dooodooom!$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 12, $$And if I put my fingers on my wrist then I can hear my pulse!$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 13, $$And I can hear myself laughing Haha haha haaah haaa!$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 14, $$And crying Boohooohooo!$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 15, $$And clapping Tap tappa tap tapaa.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 16, $$And most of all - I can hear my stomach rumbling Guddu guddu guddu...$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 17, $$And saying Feed me, feed me.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 18, $$And my nose can hear jalebis frying in mother’s kitchen.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 19, $$It is fun listening to my body. And now I want to hear my jaws chewing.$$),
    ('46326cbb-ba36-4691-9754-c1585bd0adc2', 20, $$And my stomach slurping on mother’s wonderful hot jalebis!$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 0, $$I am Maria.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 1, $$This is my mother.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 2, $$This is our baby.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 3, $$This is my father.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 4, $$This is my brother.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 5, $$This is my sister.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 6, $$This is my grandmother.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 7, $$This is my grandfather.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 8, $$This is my uncle.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 9, $$This is my aunt.$$),
    ('468f071b-8251-4554-9e6f-21bfd9c5e57d', 10, $$This is my family!$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 0, $$A crocodile has sharp teeth.$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 1, $$A lion has sharp teeth as well.$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 2, $$A shark has very sharp teeth! Why do some animals have sharp teeth?$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 3, $$A cow has strong teeth for grinding.$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 4, $$A bird does not have teeth. How does a bird eat?$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 5, $$Rats have big front teeth.$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 6, $$I used to have front teeth.$$),
    ('47dbea42-21c8-41d6-bd15-3718fe81bdbf', 7, $$My front teeth fell out!$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 0, $$Luwo went to church with his mother. She was holding his hand on the path.$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 1, $$Inside the church there were many people gathered. They were singing.$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 2, $$Luwo left the church. His mother didn’t even see him.$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 3, $$Luwo stood in the path. He looked down the path and thought, “Where is my house? ”$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 4, $$So he followed the path. He saw a big house. “No, that’s not our house. Our house is small. ”$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 5, $$Luwo walked a bit more. He saw a house on stilts. “No, that’s not our house. Our house is not up on stilts. ”$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 6, $$He kept on walking. He saw a small house of straw. “No, that’s not our house. Our house has mud walls. ”$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 7, $$Luwo went farther. He saw a small house with a mango tree outside. “No, that’s not our house. Our house has two mango trees outside. ”$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 8, $$At last Luwo saw his mother coming toward him. Luwo ran to his mother. His mother said, “Let’s go home! ”$$),
    ('495f6e13-3884-4a70-9e02-50918551e860', 9, $$Which house is Luwo’s house?$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 0, $$Once upon a time, there lived a man called Joel in Aya village.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 1, $$He did not mind of storing food for future use, but waste them.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 2, $$Nothing was left in the granary.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 3, $$Maize plants wilted and dried up.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 4, $$A strong wind blew off the granary roof.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 5, $$Children scramble for little food left in the saucepan.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 6, $$Mother laid flat down crying about what to give to the children next time.$$),
    ('4c88d493-a3e0-437a-8ee5-7599be7a2b3c', 7, $$Father sat under the veranda thinking about the future.$$)
  ) AS v(source_id, page_index, text)
  JOIN books b
    ON b.source_platform = 'bloom' AND b.source_id = v.source_id
ON CONFLICT (book_id, page_index) DO NOTHING;

-- ───────── [적재검증] 트랜잭션 안 ─────────
-- (c) 적재 후 행 수 — 기대 448
